Notebook[{
Cell["Lesson 12 - Oracle and Stages", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"fefeaf40-d546-450a-85a2-c1ef9adabc14"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two tools that sit beside the pipeline rather than in it. ",
 StyleBox["Oracle",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " checks the assembled equations numerically, by a route that shares nothing \
with Propagator, Projection, FrequencyIntegration and Assemble. ",
 StyleBox["Stages",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " saves any stage to disk and loads it back, refusing a file that is stale."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"68f4ae05-3d37-4ff4-9f50-adfc48cab7fc"],

Cell["\<\
Get[\"~/Physics/Sources/FRGscalarMSR/FRGscalarMSR.wl\"];
Get[FileNameJoin[{$FRGRoot, \"lessons\", \"LessonSetup.wl\"}]];
equations = lessonUpTo[\"Equations\"];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b61a7b65-10e6-490e-add1-183e705f0a59"],

Cell["1. The oracle", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"56b475c1-26bd-4895-af22-673a2ad86570"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["What it does.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " At one random point (couplings, ",
 StyleBox["dsCoupling[c]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", k random; each shape a concrete function such as 1/(1 + y",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ") or e^{",
 StyleBox["\[Minus]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "y}; d = 2 and 3; an explicit loop momentum vector), it builds ",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalGamma]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "2 + R as a numerical matrix, inverts it, evaluates the loop trace of lesson \
07, integrates it over ",
 StyleBox["\[Omega]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " with ",
 StyleBox["NIntegrate",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", and takes the frequency and momentum projections by finite differences. \
The result must agree with the symbolic integrand at the same point."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e792495f-5c07-4df6-b07a-ba5fea93c2dd"],

Cell["oracle = RunOracle[equations, \"ZeroFlows\" -> True];", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a93ce67a-e2c2-4bab-abad-5fa5ecb0da01"],

Cell["\<\
20 comparisons: 2 equations and 8 flows that must vanish, in d = 2 and d = 3. \
One of them in detail:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1afb46f5-ce0c-4444-af3c-670153a0a3fb"],

Cell["oracle[\"Results\"][[1]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"36fa851c-a326-4fdd-816c-029ee5b67962"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Why it's built this way: A numerical oracle beside an exact \
pipeline",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\n\n",
 "Every symbolic module checks itself, but a check written by the same hand \
as the code can share its blind spots. The oracle answers the question \"are \
these equations right?\" by brute force: no atoms, no residues, no direction \
averages, no compact forms, just numbers. Agreement to 10",
 StyleBox["\:207b\.b2\:2070",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " at a random point of a rational function is as strong as evidence gets. \
Its blind spot is stated on the card (ASSUMPTION ",
 StyleBox["Oracle.scope",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 "): it uses the same vertices and the same loop formula, so it cannot test \
the normalisation of lesson 07. That is what the Canet comparison (lesson 11, \
last exercise) is for."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.55],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.93, 0.93, 0.93],ExpressionUUID->"2efdfd35-2d73-46b3-974c-dcd7f57c5a77"],

Cell["2. How the oracle computes", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4a201dd3-fce2-4d09-a7ef-d66c775a32c6"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Oracle.wl:19-20 *)
(* concrete shapes for the numerical point, as in the script's randomPoint *)
oracleShapes = {Function[y, 1/(1 + y^2)], Function[y, Exp[-y]], Function[y, \
2/(2 + y)], Function[y, 1/(1 + y)], Function[y, 3/(3 + y^2)]};\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"cf48d925-5b4a-4ffb-a174-ba35bb780ec8"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Oracle.wl:25-32 *)
oraclePoint[eqs_, seed_, d_] := Module[{cps = eqs[\"Couplings\"], dsc, pt},
   dsc = dsCoupling /@ cps;
   SeedRandom[seed];
   pt = Join[Thread[cps -> RandomInteger[{1, 30}, Length[cps]]/17], \
Thread[dsc -> RandomInteger[{-30, 30}, Length[dsc]]/17],
     {eqs[\"Scale\"] -> RandomInteger[{10, 30}]/17, eqs[\"Dimension\"] -> d},
     MapIndexed[#1 -> oracleShapes[[Mod[#2[[1]] - 1, Length[oracleShapes]] + \
1]] &, eqs[\"Shapes\"]],
     MapIndexed[#1 -> oracleFunctions[[Mod[#2[[1]] - 1, \
Length[oracleFunctions]] + 1]] &, Lookup[eqs, \"MomentumFunctions\", {}]]];
   pt];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"3e87434c-04a1-46ec-a337-6e84d9b7faf6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["MapIndexed[f, list]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " calls ",
 StyleBox["f[element, {position}]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", so the i-th shape of your regulator gets the i-th concrete function (",
 StyleBox["Mod",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " wraps around if there are more shapes than functions)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"13ee6742-a207-4fe4-a000-800dc55aac6d"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Oracle.wl:88-108 *)
      (* numeric Gamma2 + R as a polynomial in w, at momentum squared x2 *)
      (* numerics per working precision wp: 40 digits (PrecisionGoal 22) for \
n = 0 as before; more for n >= 1, where 2n-th
         differences at h = 10^-5 eat 10 n digits (reviews E3, E15: the \
precision is part of every memo key) *)
      mat[wp_] := mat[wp] = N[(Gamma2Matrix[v, wO, xO] /. scal[xO, xO] -> \
x2O) + RegulatorMatrix[reg, x2O] /. pt, wp + 10];
      gNum[w_, x2_, wp_] := Inverse[mat[wp] /. {wO -> w, x2O -> x2}];
      vecs = {qO -> qVec, pO -> pVecO};
      dot[e_] := e /. {scal[a_, b_] :> ((a /. vecs) . (b /. vecs)), wedge[a_, \
b_] :> wedgeN[a /. vecs, b /. vecs]};
      g3[i_, {nu_, p_}, {w_, q_}, wp_] := g3[i, {nu, p}, {w, q}, wp] = \
N[dot[Gamma3Matrix[v, i, {nu, p}, {w, q}]] /. pt, wp + 10];
      g4[a_, b_, wp_] := g4[a, b, wp] = N[dot[Table[VertexValue[v, {a, b, c, \
e}, {{nuO, pO}, {-nuO, -pO}, {wO, qO}}], {c, fields}, {e, fields}]] /. pt, wp \
+ 10];
      dsr[wp_] := dsr[wp] = N[DsRegulatorMatrix[reg, q2] /. pt, wp + 10];
      (* the loop at external (nu, pVec), integrated over w: the same trace \
formula as Loops *)
      fLoop[{a_, b_}, nu_, pVec_, {wp_, pg_}] := memo[{a, b}, nu, pVec, {wp, \
pg}] = Module[{g0, gm, tr},
         g0 = gNum[wO, q2, wp]; gm = gNum[wO + nu, (pVec + qVec) . (pVec + \
qVec), wp];
         tr = Tr[dsr[wp] . g0 . (g3[a, {nuO, pO}, {wO, qO}, wp] /. {nuO -> \
nu, pVecO -> pVec}) . gm .
             (g3[b, {-nuO, -pO}, {wO + nuO, pO + qO}, wp] /. {nuO -> nu, \
pVecO -> pVec}) . g0];
         If[hasG4, tr = tr - Tr[dsr[wp] . g0 . (g4[a, b, wp] /. {nuO -> nu, \
pVecO -> pVec}) . g0]/2];
         (* a rational function of w with numeric coefficients; AccuracyGoal \
stops the search on integrands that vanish *)
         tr = Together[tr/(2 Pi)];
         If[Chop[tr, 10^-(wp - 5)] === 0, 0,
         Quiet[NIntegrate[tr, {wO, -Infinity, -10, 0, 10, Infinity}, \
WorkingPrecision -> wp, PrecisionGoal -> pg, AccuracyGoal -> wp - 8, \
MaxRecursion -> 30],
          {NIntegrate::izero, NIntegrate::precw}]]];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"40d7f1c7-2e5d-4397-aa0e-b4715511d259"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Mathematica: Arbitrary precision",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\n",
 StyleBox["N[x, n]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " gives n digits, in software arithmetic that tracks its own precision; ",
 StyleBox["Chop[x, eps]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " replaces numbers smaller than eps by 0.",
 "\n\n",
 "Machine numbers have about 16 digits. The finite differences of the oracle, \
with h = 10",
 StyleBox["\:207b\:2075",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ", lose about 10 digits per second derivative, so every number is computed \
with 40 or more digits: ",
 StyleBox["N[..., wp + 10]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " for the matrices, ",
 StyleBox["WorkingPrecision -> wp",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " for the integral. ",
 StyleBox["Inverse[m]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " inverts a numerical (or symbolic) matrix."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.3, 0.5, 0.85],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.91, 0.95, 1.],ExpressionUUID->"5a4ec72b-fef1-4cb3-97dd-c4ead13cf52f"],

Cell["\<\
{N[Pi, 30], Chop[10.^-20 + 1. - 1.], Inverse[{{1, 2}, {3, 4}}]}\
\>", "Input",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.3, 0.5, 0.85],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.91, 0.95, 1.],ExpressionUUID->"616df494-566a-49a5-9cbe-63c481faefa9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Mathematica: NIntegrate",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\n",
 StyleBox["NIntegrate[f, {x, a, b}]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " integrates numerically; ",
 StyleBox["PrecisionGoal",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["AccuracyGoal",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " set the relative and absolute target, ",
 StyleBox["WorkingPrecision",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " the digits used.",
 "\n\n",
 StyleBox["{wO, -Infinity, -10, 0, 10, Infinity}",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " splits the real axis at the given points, which helps the integrator. ",
 StyleBox["AccuracyGoal -> wp - 8",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " lets it stop on integrands that vanish, where a relative goal could never \
be met. ",
 StyleBox["Quiet[..., {NIntegrate::izero, NIntegrate::precw}]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " (",
 StyleBox["Check and Quiet",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 StyleBox[" (Glossary, lesson 00)",
  FontSlant->Italic,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.4]],
 ") silences two expected messages and no others."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.3, 0.5, 0.85],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.91, 0.95, 1.],ExpressionUUID->"1fedcb89-c787-44b1-8565-bf904370daf0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The memo keys of ",
 StyleBox["mat",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["g3",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["dsr",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["fLoop",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
